1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,546
Ravi's second Chai Corner
opens in two weeks.

2
00:00:03,846 --> 00:00:05,283
The stoves are ready.

3
00:00:05,283 --> 00:00:06,627
The cups are ready.

4
00:00:06,627 --> 00:00:08,653
But nobody is there to run it.

5
00:00:09,203 --> 00:00:12,332
Last year, Ravi hired the
first person who asked.

6
00:00:12,632 --> 00:00:15,825
That helper came late, burnt
the milk, and quit in a week.

7
00:00:16,125 --> 00:00:20,473
This time, three jobs need filling,
and there is no room for mistakes.

8
00:00:21,123 --> 00:00:22,787
More hands are not enough.

9
00:00:22,787 --> 00:00:24,451
He needs the right people.

10
00:00:25,151 --> 00:00:26,466
So, what is staffing?

11
00:00:26,766 --> 00:00:30,705
Staffing means filling every job
with the right person, and keeping it

12
00:00:30,705 --> 00:00:31,605
filled.

13
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:35,698
Keeping it filled matters, because
people leave, grow, and move up.

14
00:00:36,348 --> 00:00:38,243
Staffing moves through eight steps.

15
00:00:38,693 --> 00:00:39,593
One.

16
00:00:39,183 --> 00:00:40,402
Manpower planning.

17
00:00:40,402 --> 00:00:42,572
How many people, and what kind?

18
00:00:42,572 --> 00:00:45,933
Ravi needs a manager, a
tea maker, and a cashier.

19
00:00:46,283 --> 00:00:47,183
Two.

20
00:00:46,821 --> 00:00:47,781
Recruitment.

21
00:00:47,781 --> 00:00:50,650
Finding people and getting them to apply.

22
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,762
They can come from two places.

23
00:00:53,062 --> 00:00:55,847
Internal sources are
people already inside.

24
00:00:55,847 --> 00:00:58,451
Meena moves up to run the new outlet.

25
00:00:58,801 --> 00:01:03,016
External sources are people from
outside, found through a notice on the

26
00:01:03,016 --> 00:01:05,229
stall, or a tip from a regular.

27
00:01:05,579 --> 00:01:07,743
Insiders already know the work.

28
00:01:07,743 --> 00:01:09,741
Outsiders bring fresh skills.

29
00:01:10,391 --> 00:01:11,291
Three.

30
00:01:10,964 --> 00:01:11,864
Selection.

31
00:01:11,725 --> 00:01:15,198
Choosing the best people,
with a test and an interview.

32
00:01:15,548 --> 00:01:18,091
Ravi's notice brings in forty people.

33
00:01:18,091 --> 00:01:19,430
That's recruitment.

34
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:21,612
Each one makes a cup of chai.

35
00:01:21,612 --> 00:01:23,435
The best ten get an interview.

36
00:01:23,785 --> 00:01:25,418
Only two get the job.

37
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:26,611
That's selection.

38
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:28,927
So recruitment is positive.

39
00:01:28,927 --> 00:01:30,295
It attracts many.

40
00:01:30,295 --> 00:01:31,929
Selection is negative.

41
00:01:31,929 --> 00:01:33,243
It rejects many.

42
00:01:33,893 --> 00:01:34,793
Four.

43
00:01:34,475 --> 00:01:36,274
Placement and orientation.

44
00:01:36,274 --> 00:01:40,775
Each person gets the right job,
and a proper welcome on day one.

45
00:01:41,125 --> 00:01:42,025
Five.

46
00:01:41,711 --> 00:01:43,469
Training and development.

47
00:01:43,469 --> 00:01:47,289
Asha teaches her recipe, so
every cup tastes the same.

48
00:01:47,639 --> 00:01:48,539
Six.

49
00:01:48,166 --> 00:01:49,684
Performance appraisal.

50
00:01:49,684 --> 00:01:52,927
A regular review of how
well each person works.

51
00:01:53,277 --> 00:01:54,177
Seven.

52
00:01:53,896 --> 00:01:55,497
Promotion and transfer.

53
00:01:55,497 --> 00:01:59,317
A star can move up, or move
across to a busier outlet.

54
00:01:59,667 --> 00:02:00,586
And eight.

55
00:02:00,586 --> 00:02:01,601
Compensation.

56
00:02:01,601 --> 00:02:04,697
Fair pay and rewards, so good people stay.

57
00:02:05,347 --> 00:02:06,281
Quick check.

58
00:02:06,281 --> 00:02:09,344
Ravi tests twenty people
and turns away eighteen.

59
00:02:09,344 --> 00:02:10,730
Which step is this?

60
00:02:12,630 --> 00:02:13,530
Selection!

61
00:02:13,377 --> 00:02:15,985
It picks the best, and rejects the rest.

62
00:02:16,585 --> 00:02:17,594
So, remember.

63
00:02:17,894 --> 00:02:22,006
Staffing means filling jobs with the
right people, and keeping them filled.

64
00:02:22,356 --> 00:02:26,766
It runs in eight steps: plan, recruit,
select, place, train, appraise,

65
00:02:26,766 --> 00:02:28,005
promote, and pay.

66
00:02:28,355 --> 00:02:30,056
Recruitment attracts many.

67
00:02:30,056 --> 00:02:31,718
Selection picks the few.

68
00:02:32,318 --> 00:02:37,029
Next time, Ravi learns to guide his team,
and make all their work fit together.
